summary:
  Ticking or unticking "This computer" beside a playing device re-reads its
  balance against the master it left instead of the one it came to.

history:
  On the default output a device alone follows the widget's volume, and
  beside this computer that volume times the room's master. The balance is
  read against the new master at the tick, so the device stays where it
  stands and the next gesture moves it from there. Read the wrong way round,
  a television at 0.15 under a room at 40 % is taken for one at full
  balance, and the first gesture after the untick sends it up to the master
  itself: a wheel step from 75 to 70 takes it from 0.15 to 0.70.

target:
  package/contents/ui/TransportLogic.js

find:
      return balanceBelow(b * was / now);

replace:
      return balanceBelow(b * now / was);

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_transportlogic.qml::test_a_device_keeps_its_level_when_this_computer_leaves
  and tests/qml/tst_volumeroad.qml::test_this_computer_leaving_does_not_send_the_television_up_at_the_next_gesture.
  Line-neutral.
